{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789838203,"nonce":"XBR0pcg+5lJwufkypVa2vdai8m8=","title":"CI: test suites, benches, nightly releases, badges","message":"Three GitHub Actions workflows: ci.yml (push/PR: the stable crates on ubuntu+macos, the whole workspace on nightly on both, the core's unit tests on wasm32-wasip1 under ash-wasm-run), bench.yml (nightly + dispatch on macos-15: the three interop benches into the run summary and an artifact; shared-runner numbers are a trend, not a measurement) and nightly.yml (nightly + dispatch: a release build of the caribou command for macos arm64/x86_64, linux x86_64/arm64 and windows msvc, packaged by scripts/package_nightly.sh the way ash's release packages ash — the runtime image beside the command under the libhl names, the haxelib, the docs — as the rolling `nightly` pre-release; skipped when HEAD is unchanged; one failing platform does not hold the others). README carries the badges.\n\nEvery job clones ash and zyntax beside caribou at the revs Cargo.toml pins (.github/actions/siblings), so the manifest is the one source of truth and the pins must be pushed revs: ash 12e6a40 and zyntax 8387b62 were not yet pushed when pinned; until they are, CI cannot resolve them. `--locked` is not used: the lock is written against the sibling trees, which run ahead of the pins.\n\nUnverified until the first runs: the Linux legs (LLVM 21 from apt.llvm.org for bindgen's libclang; ash_std, wren_lift, zyntax on x86_64/arm64 Linux), the Windows leg (bindgen against the runner image's libclang; whether the core and the adapters build for msvc at all), macos-15-intel. Verified locally on macOS arm64: the stable core command, the workspace tests, the release build, the packaging script and the packaged command running hud.hl from a clean directory (system dylibs only).\n\nNot gated: clippy (immix.rs carries pre-existing lints) and rustfmt (nightly rustfmt rewrites `pub use` lists stable leaves alone). Private repository: the badges render for members; Actions minutes are billed, macOS at its multiplier.","files":null}]}